{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-22471","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-22805","text":"PRISM × box-and-box — Arithmetic Integration Review"}]},{"id":"blk-22472","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22806","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status:"},{"id":"spn-22807","text":" review (no scoring break) · "},{"id":"spn-22808","marks":["bold"],"text":"Kernel:"},{"id":"spn-22809","text":" "},{"id":"spn-22810","marks":["code"],"text":"box-and-box"},{"id":"spn-22811","text":" v0.8.0 (8 rungs, 97 laws) "},{"id":"spn-22812","marks":["bold"],"text":"Scope:"},{"id":"spn-22813","text":" how the PRISM benchmark engine (OS-009) relates to the [&] governance kernel, which parts of the scoring pipeline are already the kernel's "},{"id":"spn-22814","marks":["bold"],"text":"axiological"},{"id":"spn-22815","text":" rung in disguise, and what additive wiring would make the correspondence exact."}]},{"id":"blk-22473","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-22816","text":"TL;DR"}]},{"id":"blk-22474","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22817","text":"PRISM "},{"id":"spn-22818","marks":["italic"],"text":"is"},{"id":"spn-22819","text":" the kernel's "},{"id":"spn-22820","marks":["bold"],"text":"axiological rung (rung 2, `score.mjs`) at scale."},{"id":"spn-22821","text":" Where the kernel ranks one decision ("},{"id":"spn-22822","marks":["code"],"text":"feasible ▸ permitted ▸ best"},{"id":"spn-22823","text":"), PRISM ranks "},{"id":"spn-22824","marks":["italic"],"text":"systems"},{"id":"spn-22825","text":" across many decisions. The two are the same algebra at different cardinalities, so the integration is mostly "},{"id":"spn-22826","marks":["bold"],"text":"naming + one optional semiring swap"},{"id":"spn-22827","text":", not a rewrite."}]},{"id":"blk-22475","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22828","text":"Three concrete touch-points, all additive:"}]},{"id":"blk-22476","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-22478","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22829","marks":["bold"],"text":"Composite scoring"},{"id":"spn-22830","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-22831","marks":["code"],"text":"Judge.Aggregator.compute_composite/2"},{"id":"spn-22832","text":") is already a"}]}],"id":"blk-22477","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-22479","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22833","marks":["bold"],"text":"probability-semiring weighted sum"},{"id":"spn-22834","text":" — name it as rung 2."}]},{"id":"blk-22480","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-22482","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22835","marks":["bold"],"text":"Meta-judge \"reject\""},{"id":"spn-22836","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-22837","marks":["code"],"text":"Judge.Aggregator.quality_weight/1"},{"id":"spn-22838","text":") is already the kernel's"}]}],"id":"blk-22481","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-22483","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22839","marks":["bold"],"text":"`0̲` annihilation / `consume()` veto"},{"id":"spn-22840","text":" — a rejected judgment is annihilated, not averaged. Name it as the deontic floor under the score."}]},{"id":"blk-22484","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-22486","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22841","marks":["bold"],"text":"Per-pass means"},{"id":"spn-22842","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-22843","marks":["code"],"text":"Sequence.Scorer.per_pass_means/1"},{"id":"spn-22844","text":") use the "},{"id":"spn-22845","marks":["italic"],"text":"arithmetic"},{"id":"spn-22846","text":" mean. An"}]}],"id":"blk-22485","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":3},{"id":"blk-22487","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22847","marks":["bold"],"text":"optional tropical-semiring (min/bottleneck) view"},{"id":"spn-22848","text":" would surface the single weakest dimension — the \"is any rung failing?\" question the kernel's safety floor asks."}]},{"id":"blk-22488","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-22849","text":"Rung-by-rung alignment"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-22490","spans":[{"id":"spn-22850","text":"Kernel rung"}]},{"id":"blk-22491","spans":[{"id":"spn-22851","text":"PRISM construct"}]},{"id":"blk-22492","spans":[{"id":"spn-22852","text":"Already aligned?"}]}],"id":"blk-22489","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-22493","spans":[{"id":"spn-22853","text":"1. alethic ("},{"id":"spn-22854","marks":["code"],"text":"value"},{"id":"spn-22855","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-22494","spans":[{"id":"spn-22856","text":"scenario/transcript = the observable facts being judged"}]},{"id":"blk-22495","spans":[{"id":"spn-22857","text":"✅ (the L1 evidence layer)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-22496","spans":[{"id":"spn-22858","text":"2. axiological ("},{"id":"spn-22859","marks":["code"],"text":"score"},{"id":"spn-22860","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-22497","spans":[{"id":"spn-22861","text":"the whole CL-dimension scoring pipeline"}]},{"id":"blk-22498","spans":[{"id":"spn-22862","text":"✅ this "},{"id":"spn-22863","marks":["italic"],"text":"is"},{"id":"spn-22864","text":" rung 2"}]}],[{"id":"blk-22499","spans":[{"id":"spn-22865","text":"3. deontic (norm/govern)"}]},{"id":"blk-22500","spans":[{"id":"spn-22866","text":"meta-judge "},{"id":"spn-22867","marks":["code"],"text":"reject"},{"id":"spn-22868","text":" → drop from aggregate (veto)"}]},{"id":"blk-22501","spans":[{"id":"spn-22869","text":"✅ approximated by "},{"id":"spn-22870","marks":["code"],"text":"quality_weight"}]}],[{"id":"blk-22502","spans":[{"id":"spn-22871","text":"4. temporal (LTL ▸ supervise)"}]},{"id":"blk-22503","spans":[{"id":"spn-22872","text":"closed-loop "},{"id":"spn-22873","marks":["code"],"text":"loop_closure_rate"},{"id":"spn-22874","text":" slope across passes"}]},{"id":"blk-22504","spans":[{"id":"spn-22875","text":"◻ partial — it's a gradient over time"}]}],[{"id":"blk-22505","spans":[{"id":"spn-22876","text":"6. epistemic (knows ▸ believes)"}]},{"id":"blk-22506","spans":[{"id":"spn-22877","text":"bootstrap confidence intervals; meta-judge audit"}]},{"id":"blk-22507","spans":[{"id":"spn-22878","text":"✅ uncertainty is first-class"}]}],[{"id":"blk-22508","spans":[{"id":"spn-22879","text":"8. resource (affine ledger)"}]},{"id":"blk-22509","spans":[{"id":"spn-22880","text":"IRT difficulty budget / cost per run"}]},{"id":"blk-22510","spans":[{"id":"spn-22881","text":"◻ implicit"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-22511","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22882","text":"(Rungs 5 reflexive and 7 strategic are out of PRISM's remit.)"}]},{"id":"blk-22512","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-22883","text":"Concrete alignments (grounded in the code)"}]},{"id":"blk-22513","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-22884","text":"1. Composite = probability-semiring weighted sum (rung 2)"}]},{"id":"blk-22514","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22885","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/prism/judge/aggregator.ex"},{"id":"spn-22886","text":" "},{"id":"spn-22887","marks":["code"],"text":"compute_composite/2"},{"id":"spn-22888","text":" (lines 93–100) computes "},{"id":"spn-22889","marks":["code"],"text":"Σ dim_score × weight"},{"id":"spn-22890","text":". That is precisely the kernel's "},{"id":"spn-22891","marks":["bold"],"text":"probability semiring"},{"id":"spn-22892","text":" in "},{"id":"spn-22893","marks":["code"],"text":"box-and-box/score.mjs"},{"id":"spn-22894","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-22895","marks":["code"],"text":"⊕ = +"},{"id":"spn-22896","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22897","marks":["code"],"text":"⊗ = ×"},{"id":"spn-22898","text":"). The CL-dimension weights in "},{"id":"spn-22899","marks":["code"],"text":"Prism.Benchmark.CLCategories.weights()"},{"id":"spn-22900","text":" are the axiological weight vector. No change needed — the recommendation is to "},{"id":"spn-22901","marks":["italic"],"text":"document"},{"id":"spn-22902","text":" that PRISM's composite is the axiological rung evaluated in the probability semiring, so the two systems share one vocabulary."}]},{"id":"blk-22515","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-22903","text":"2. Meta-judge reject = "},{"id":"spn-22904","marks":["code"],"text":"0̲"},{"id":"spn-22905","text":" annihilation (deontic floor under the score)"}]},{"id":"blk-22516","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22906","marks":["code"],"text":"quality_weight/1"},{"id":"spn-22907","text":" (lines 131–137) maps a meta-judge recommendation to a weight, and "},{"id":"spn-22908","marks":["code"],"text":"aggregate/3"},{"id":"spn-22909","text":" (line 40) then "},{"id":"spn-22910","marks":["bold"],"text":"filters out"},{"id":"spn-22911","text":" any judgment whose quality weight is "},{"id":"spn-22912","marks":["code"],"text":"0.0"},{"id":"spn-22913","text":". That filter is exactly the kernel's "},{"id":"spn-22914","marks":["bold"],"text":"`consume()` veto / `0̲` annihilation"},{"id":"spn-22915","text":": a rejected judgment does not get "},{"id":"spn-22916","marks":["italic"],"text":"down-weighted and averaged in"},{"id":"spn-22917","text":", it is "},{"id":"spn-22918","marks":["bold"],"text":"annihilated"},{"id":"spn-22919","text":" — removed from the aggregate entirely. This is the deontic safety floor: a verdict that violates the floor cannot be \"made up for\" by strong scores elsewhere. PRISM already does the right thing; naming it as the "},{"id":"spn-22920","marks":["code"],"text":"0̲"},{"id":"spn-22921","text":" rule makes the guarantee legible and testable against law "},{"id":"spn-22922","marks":["code"],"text":"DB2"},{"id":"spn-22923","text":" (annihilation) in the kernel's deontic suite."}]},{"id":"blk-22517","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-22924","text":"3. Per-pass mean: add an optional tropical (bottleneck) view"}]},{"id":"blk-22518","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22925","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/prism/sequence/scorer.ex"},{"id":"spn-22926","text":" "},{"id":"spn-22927","marks":["code"],"text":"per_pass_means/1"},{"id":"spn-22928","text":" (lines 82–92) takes the "},{"id":"spn-22929","marks":["bold"],"text":"arithmetic mean"},{"id":"spn-22930","text":" of dimension scores. That answers \"how good on average?\" The kernel's safety floor asks a different question — \"is "},{"id":"spn-22931","marks":["italic"],"text":"any"},{"id":"spn-22932","text":" rung failing?\" — which is the "},{"id":"spn-22933","marks":["bold"],"text":"tropical semiring"},{"id":"spn-22934","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-22935","marks":["code"],"text":"⊕ = min"},{"id":"spn-22936","text":") in "},{"id":"spn-22937","marks":["code"],"text":"score.mjs"},{"id":"spn-22938","text":". An "},{"id":"spn-22939","marks":["italic"],"text":"additive"},{"id":"spn-22940","text":" "},{"id":"spn-22941","marks":["code"],"text":"per_pass_floor/1"},{"id":"spn-22942","text":" companion (the min across dimensions per pass) would expose the bottleneck dimension without touching the existing mean-based metrics. This is the single most useful optional wiring: it turns \"average CL competence\" into \"average "},{"id":"spn-22943","marks":["bold"],"text":"and"},{"id":"spn-22944","text":" weakest-link CL competence,\" matching how the bridge gates on the floor before optimizing the gradient."}]},{"id":"blk-22519","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-22945","text":"4. Loop closure slope = the axiological gradient over time (rung 2 ▸ rung 4)"}]},{"id":"blk-22520","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22946","marks":["code"],"text":"loop_closure_rate/1"},{"id":"spn-22947","text":" (lines 36–40) is the linear-regression slope of per-pass means — literally the "},{"id":"spn-22948","marks":["bold"],"text":"gradient"},{"id":"spn-22949","text":" the kernel's bridge optimizes in its "},{"id":"spn-22950","marks":["code"],"text":"best"},{"id":"spn-22951","text":" step, but measured "},{"id":"spn-22952","marks":["italic"],"text":"across time"},{"id":"spn-22953","text":" (which makes it also a temporal-rung, rung-4, liveness signal: \"does the system eventually improve?\"). No change; worth citing the correspondence so \"loop closure\" and \"the best gradient\" are understood as the same quantity at different timescales."}]},{"id":"blk-22521","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-22954","text":"Suggested (optional, additive) wiring"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-22523","spans":[{"id":"spn-22955","text":"Change"}]},{"id":"blk-22524","spans":[{"id":"spn-22956","text":"File"}]},{"id":"blk-22525","spans":[{"id":"spn-22957","text":"Risk"}]},{"id":"blk-22526","spans":[{"id":"spn-22958","text":"Value"}]}],"id":"blk-22522","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-22527","spans":[{"id":"spn-22959","text":"Document composite = probability semiring"}]},{"id":"blk-22528","spans":[{"id":"spn-22960","marks":["code"],"text":"aggregator.ex"},{"id":"spn-22961","text":" moduledoc"}]},{"id":"blk-22529","spans":[{"id":"spn-22962","text":"none"}]},{"id":"blk-22530","spans":[{"id":"spn-22963","text":"shared vocabulary"}]}],[{"id":"blk-22531","spans":[{"id":"spn-22964","text":"Name reject-filter as "},{"id":"spn-22965","marks":["code"],"text":"0̲"},{"id":"spn-22966","text":" annihilation"}]},{"id":"blk-22532","spans":[{"id":"spn-22967","marks":["code"],"text":"aggregator.ex"},{"id":"spn-22968","text":" "},{"id":"spn-22969","marks":["code"],"text":"quality_weight/1"},{"id":"spn-22970","text":" doc"}]},{"id":"blk-22533","spans":[{"id":"spn-22971","text":"none"}]},{"id":"blk-22534","spans":[{"id":"spn-22972","text":"legible safety floor"}]}],[{"id":"blk-22535","spans":[{"id":"spn-22973","text":"Add "},{"id":"spn-22974","marks":["code"],"text":"per_pass_floor/1"},{"id":"spn-22975","text":" (tropical/min view)"}]},{"id":"blk-22536","spans":[{"id":"spn-22976","marks":["code"],"text":"sequence/scorer.ex"}]},{"id":"blk-22537","spans":[{"id":"spn-22977","text":"low (new fn)"}]},{"id":"blk-22538","spans":[{"id":"spn-22978","text":"bottleneck visibility"}]}],[{"id":"blk-22539","spans":[{"id":"spn-22979","text":"Cite loop-closure ↔ best-gradient"}]},{"id":"blk-22540","spans":[{"id":"spn-22980","marks":["code"],"text":"sequence/scorer.ex"},{"id":"spn-22981","text":" moduledoc"}]},{"id":"blk-22541","spans":[{"id":"spn-22982","text":"none"}]},{"id":"blk-22542","spans":[{"id":"spn-22983","text":"conceptual unification"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-22543","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22984","text":"None of these change existing outputs, leaderboards, or the 9-dimension weights."}]},{"id":"blk-22544","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-22985","text":"What this review deliberately does NOT do"}]},{"id":"blk-22545","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-22547","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22986","text":"It does "},{"id":"spn-22987","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-22988","text":" swap the arithmetic mean for tropical by default — the existing composite"}]}],"id":"blk-22546","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-22548","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22989","text":"and per-pass-mean metrics are preserved exactly; tropical is an "},{"id":"spn-22990","marks":["italic"],"text":"additional"},{"id":"spn-22991","text":" view."}]},{"id":"blk-22549","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-22551","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22992","text":"It does "},{"id":"spn-22993","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-22994","text":" re-weight any CL dimension or alter IRT calibration."}]}],"id":"blk-22550","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-22553","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22995","text":"It does "},{"id":"spn-22996","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-22997","text":" make PRISM call into the JS kernel at runtime (the kernel is a spec/ref;"}]}],"id":"blk-22552","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-22554","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22998","text":"PRISM stays self-contained Elixir)."}]},{"id":"blk-22555","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-22999","text":"Reference"}]},{"id":"blk-22556","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-22558","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23000","marks":["code"],"text":"AmpersandBoxDesign/box-and-box/score.mjs"},{"id":"spn-23001","text":" — semirings (tropical/probability/log)"}]}],"id":"blk-22557","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-22560","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23002","marks":["code"],"text":"AmpersandBoxDesign/box-and-box/bridge.mjs"},{"id":"spn-23003","text":" — floor-then-gradient, "},{"id":"spn-23004","marks":["code"],"text":"consume()"},{"id":"spn-23005","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23006","marks":["code"],"text":"0̲"}]}],"id":"blk-22559","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-22562","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23007","marks":["code"],"text":"AmpersandBoxDesign/docs/CC2-capability-composition.md"},{"id":"spn-23008","text":" — operators × arithmetics"}]}],"id":"blk-22561","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-22564","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23009","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/prism/judge/aggregator.ex"},{"id":"spn-23010","text":" — composite + meta-judge veto (this review's §1–2)"}]}],"id":"blk-22563","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-22566","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23011","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/prism/sequence/scorer.ex"},{"id":"spn-23012","text":" — per-pass means + loop closure (this review's §3–4)"}]}],"id":"blk-22565","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaiera7adlba3vrsx2cqjmh7mszfhfkbv5aqbtgius37iznkort6dxwaia","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}